+# NEB v0.1 — explicit nonlinear orbital trapping
+
+For the six balanced phase-branch embeddings, every finite r>=1 and a,N>0 on 0<epsilon<=10^-5, set m=min(a,N*epsilon)/2, J=max(a,25*N), R=3*m/(62*N), B=m*R^2/2 and delta=R*sqrt(m/(2*J)). In the declared Frobenius/round-sphere product metric, initial orbit distance <=delta guarantees energy excess <=B/2 and orbit distance <R for all time. Distance <R plus energy excess <B is a second sufficient criterion. A target-dependent stability modulus is explicit for every target <=R.
+
+The new replay certifies the scalar Schur floor C_phase>2*epsilon*I on 64 rigorous interval cells (211 exact/interval checks total). The proof converts it to a full orbit-normal Hessian floor and bounds global geodesic second and third energy derivatives by max(a,25*N) and 62*N. Six synthetic matrix/sphere jet fixtures check the formulas numerically. Eight manuscript pages rendered, decoded and visually inspected.
+
+For a=N=1 and epsilon=10^-5: R=3/12400000 (about 2.41935e-7), B=9/61504000000000000000 (about 1.46332e-19), delta about 7.65067e-11. These are conservative mathematical guarantees, not physical tolerances. The endpoint epsilon=0 and maximal basin remain open quantitatively. Development, no registry entry. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0.
